---
import DesignPage from '../../components/DesignPage.astro';
import { radii, shadows } from '../../lib/tokens';

const widths = [
  { name: 'sm', value: '48rem', note: 'prose, forms' },
  { name: 'md', value: '64rem', note: 'content' },
  { name: 'lg', value: '72rem', note: 'the default section measure' },
  { name: 'xl', value: '80rem', note: 'wide layouts, the header bar' },
  { name: 'full', value: 'none', note: 'edge to edge' },
];
---

<DesignPage title="Shape" description="There is no --ds- token for shape. What follows are Tailwind theme variables that tokens.css sets in its @theme block, reached through the usual utilities (rounded-md, shadow-lg), and the measures are Tailwind's max-w steps. A theme that wants another geometry overrides these variables or, as Corporate and Minimal do, flattens everything with one rule. Whether shape should become roles of the system is an open question this page exists to settle.">
  <section class="mb-12" aria-labelledby="radii">
    <h2 id="radii" class="docs-ui type-h2 mb-2">Radii</h2>
    <p class="docs-ui mb-4 text-sm text-muted">{radii.length} Tailwind theme variables, set by <code>tokens.css</code>. Buttons and badges use <code>rounded-full</code>; cards, dialogs and inputs <code>rounded-md</code> to <code>rounded-xl</code>.</p>
    <div class="docs-preview rounded-lg border border-(--doc-border) p-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6">
        {radii.map((r) => (
          <div class="text-center">
            <span class="mx-auto block size-16 border-2 border-primary bg-primary-soft" style={`border-radius: var(${r.name})`}></span>
            <span class="mt-2 block font-mono text-xs text-heading">{r.name}</span>
            <span class="block font-mono text-[10px] text-muted">{r.value} · {r.name.replace('--radius-', 'rounded-')}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12" aria-labelledby="shadows">
    <h2 id="shadows" class="docs-ui type-h2 mb-2">Shadows</h2>
    <p class="docs-ui mb-4 text-sm text-muted">{shadows.length} Tailwind theme variables, set by <code>tokens.css</code>. Cards take <code>shadow-sm</code>; menus, popovers and dialogs <code>shadow-lg</code>.</p>
    <div class="docs-preview rounded-lg border border-(--doc-border) p-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-8">
        {shadows.map((s) => (
          <div class="text-center">
            <span class="mx-auto block size-20 rounded-lg bg-surface" style={`box-shadow: var(${s.name})`}></span>
            <span class="mt-3 block font-mono text-xs text-heading">{s.name}</span>
            <span class="block font-mono text-[10px] text-muted">{s.name.replace('--shadow-', 'shadow-')}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <table class="mt-6 w-full text-xs">
        <thead><tr class="text-left text-muted"><th class="py-1 pr-4">Variable</th><th class="py-1">Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{shadows.map((s) => <tr class="border-t border-border"><td class="py-1 pr-4 font-mono text-heading whitespace-nowrap">{s.name}</td><td class="py-1 font-mono text-muted">{s.value}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12" aria-labelledby="measure">
    <h2 id="measure" class="docs-ui type-h2 mb-2">Measures</h2>
    <p class="docs-ui mb-4 text-sm text-muted">The Container element owns the horizontal measure; sections pick one of five. These are Tailwind's <code>max-w-*</code> steps, not tokens, which is deliberate: a theme changes colour and type, not the page grid.</p>
    <div class="docs-ui overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead><tr class="text-left text-muted"><th class="px-4 py-2">width</th><th class="px-4 py-2">max</th><th class="px-4 py-2">For</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{widths.map((w) => <tr class="border-t border-border"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-heading">{w.name}</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-muted">{w.value}</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted">{w.note}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12" aria-labelledby="motion">
    <h2 id="motion" class="docs-ui type-h2 mb-2">Motion</h2>
    <p class="docs-ui text-sm text-muted">There are no motion tokens. Transitions live in each element's own CSS, under <code>prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference</code>, and never carry function: the reduced-motion pass of the gate proves every element works with them off. Durations are 150 to 250 ms.</p>
  </section>
</DesignPage>
